I recently wrote a small test module connecting to QGC from MAVSDK, pretending to be an autopilot. I found a few issues in MAVSDK, that I patched [here](https://github.com/Auterion/fake_autopilot/blob/master/mavsdk.patch).

More specifically, MAVSDK ignores messages coming from QGC...

1. ... in [receive_message()](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/develop/src/core/mavsdk_impl.cpp#L78-L84):

```cpp
    // FIXME: Ignore messages from QGroundControl for now. Usually QGC identifies
    //        itself with sysid 255.
    //        A better way would probably be to parse the heartbeat message and
    //        look at type and check if it is MAV_TYPE_GCS.
    if (message.sysid == 255) {
        return;
    }
```

