> So if u could please guide me about how we are receiving callbacks.
> 
> telemetry.subscribe_position([](Telemetry::Position position) {
> std::cout << "Altitude: " << position.relative_altitude_m << " m\n";
> });
> 
> Here why are we passing Telemetry::Position not telemetry::Position because we have initiated the system plugin by ""auto telemetry = Telemetry{system};""

This is a C++ question - these bug reports are for MAVSDK library issues.

`Telemetry::Position` is a data type. The instances you have created (`telemetry1` `telemetry2`) affect only how you setup the subscription.

```
// Setup for telemetry 1
telemetry1.subscribe_position([](Telemetry::Position position) {
std::cout << "Altitude 1: " << position.relative_altitude_m << " \n";
});`

// Setup for telemetry 2
telemetry2.subscribe_position([](Telemetry::Position position) {
std::cout << "Altitude 2: " << position.relative_altitude_m << " \n";
});
```

The only difference is the variable you call `subscribe_position` onto :)

https://stackoverflow.com/questions/7627098/what-is-a-lambda-expression-in-c11

