Hi,

For my projects needs, I had to implement messages forwarding.
An example use case is:
- 245.190 = Ground Control Station (GCS)
- 1.195 = Companion Computer (CC)
- 1.1 = PX4 Autopilot (PX4)

CC is connected to the GCS (UDP) and to the PX4 (serial).
We need the GCS to be able to send command/messages directly to the PX4.

Thus, I have added messages forwarding functionality based on PX4 source code.
The forward_message function was adapted from Firmware v1.11.3:
    https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/blob/v1.11.3/src/modules/mavlink/mavlink_main.cpp#L460

See changes in: [add-messages-forwarding](/yhabib29/MAVSDK/tree/add-messages-forwarding)

I had to keep track of the origin connection from which the message was received to ignore it when forwarding.
There might be a better way to do this.

```diff --git a/src/core/connection.h b/src/core/connection.h
index 02ba17b4..5b977325 100644
--- a/src/core/connection.h
+++ b/src/core/connection.h
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ namespace mavsdk {
 
 class Connection {
 public:
-    typedef std::function<void(mavlink_message_t& message)> receiver_callback_t;
+    typedef std::function<void(mavlink_message_t& message, Connection *connection)> receiver_callback_t;
 
     Connection(receiver_callback_t receiver_callback);
     virtual ~Connection();
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ public:
 protected:
     bool start_mavlink_receiver();
     void stop_mavlink_receiver();
-    void receive_message(mavlink_message_t& message);
+    void receive_message(mavlink_message_t& message, Connection *connection);
 
     receiver_callback_t _receiver_callback{};
     std::unique_ptr<MAVLinkReceiver> _mavlink_receiver;
```


If this feature is useful to you, I can make a pull request.
However, i did not update the integration tests, etc ...

When heartbeat timeout happens, `disable()` is called on all plugins. In case of `MissionRawImpl` plugin, this will call the `reset_mission_progress()` method which clears the current mission state. After reconnect, this state is no longer known and functions such as `set_current_mission_item_async()` will not work due to the following check:

```
if (index < 0 || index >= _mission_progress.last.total) { // <--- _mission_progress.last.total is set to 0 on lost heartbeat 
        _system_impl->call_user_callback([callback]() {
            if (callback) {
                callback(MissionRaw::Result::InvalidArgument);
                return;
            }
        });
    }
```

This is quite confusing behavior, as vehicle refuses to change the mission to another waypoint even if connection is reestablished and everything else seems to work fine. 

A possible fix is to reimplement `MissionRawImpl::disable()` and `MissionRawImpl::enable()` to simply set a flag within the _mission_progress. This flag would then be checked before trying to change any state and only proceed if connection is established.

