> I do not observer the variable "want_to_pause" be reset to "false"; thereby this interruption will occur only once at mission_progress.current ==2, i.e. mission >=3 will not call this interruption , is it right? How do I enable the pause properly, change "want_to_pause" variable back to "false" at line L263?

It's only set to `true` once, correct.

You could also call it at every waypoint like this:

```
    mission.subscribe_mission_progress([&want_to_pause](Mission::MissionProgress mission_progress) {
        want_to_pause = true;
    });
```

Then you would have to reset it somewhere else, e.g.
```
while (!want_to_pause) {
    sleep_for(seconds(1));
}
want_to_pause = false;
```

> During the pause process, I can use the offboard mode ?

Yes you can. Pause just means it goes to Hold/Loiter mode.

> The code L228-230 concerning " while (!want_to_pause)" serves for which reason? It has any connection with the interruption ?

This waits until the flag is set to `true`.

